<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (Ok ladies, one thing I think we can all agree on, the term "big emotions" can be triggering. Many of us are all too familiar with "why are you being so emotional" or "why are women so emotional," so we have been wired to suppress our emotions. And I get it. When you've been made to feel like your emotions are a problem, spending years trying to suppress them makes complete sense.)
/E (Ok ladies, one thing I think we can all agree on, the term "big emotions" can be triggering. Many of us are all too familiar with "why are you being so emotional" or "why are women so emotional," so we have been wired to suppress our emotions. And I get it. When you've been made to feel like your emotions are a problem, spending years trying to suppress them makes complete sense.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
568 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (So I need you to hear this: your ability to feel, to empathize, to care deeply, that is one of the most beautiful things about you. Big emotions aren't a malfunction. They're information, messengers knocking to tell you something matters. The goal was never to feel calm all the time. It's to stop being afraid of your own feelings, so they can move through you instead of running the show.)
/E (So I need you to hear this: your ability to feel, to empathize, to care deeply, that is one of the most beautiful things about you. Big emotions aren't a malfunction. They're information, messengers knocking to tell you something matters. The goal was never to feel calm all the time. It's to stop being afraid of your own feelings, so they can move through you instead of running the show.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
569 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (Most of us were taught two options: explode or numb. But there's a third way nobody teaches, feel it, on purpose, with support. Emotions are like waves. They rise, they crest, and if you let them, they pass. Numbing doesn't end the wave; it just makes you brace against it forever.)
/E (Most of us were taught two options: explode or numb. But there's a third way nobody teaches, feel it, on purpose, with support. Emotions are like waves. They rise, they crest, and if you let them, they pass. Numbing doesn't end the wave; it just makes you brace against it forever.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
